debark: unknown flag: --nonexistent-flag

Usage:
  debark verify BUNDLE [flags]

Flags:
      --allow-unsigned        accept a bundle with no valid signature (must be an explicit choice)
      --gpg-keyring string    gpg keyring FILE holding the expected release key(s), for gpg-signed bundles; without it gpg uses this machine's default keyring
  -h, --help                  help for verify
      --key stringArray       operator public key file; repeatable
      --keyring stringArray   directory of trusted public keys; repeatable

Global Flags:
      --config string        config file path (overrides XDG discovery)
      --json                 print the documented JSON object for this command instead of human text
      --json-events string   stream NDJSON evidence events to PATH, or "-" for stdout
      --no-color             disable coloured output (also honours NO_COLOR and TERM=dumb)
      --profile string       named config profile to apply
